1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:05,620
Meet ai and ay — two best friends who make the same sound!

2
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:07,570
They both say...

3
00:00:08,020 --> 00:00:08,960
ayyy!

4
00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:09,760
Like in rain...

5
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:10,940
and play!

6
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:13,380
But if they sound the same...

7
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:15,760
how do you know which one to use?

8
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:20,720
Here's the secret — little i is very shy.

9
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:26,400
She never sits at the end of a word, so ai stays in the middle.

10
00:00:27,580 --> 00:00:31,160
But y is brave — y loves being last!

11
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:34,840
So ay goes at the end of a word.

12
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:37,500
Let's try some more words!

13
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:39,160
Snail...

14
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:40,840
train...

15
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:42,960
ai is in the middle.

16
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:44,600
Play...

17
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:45,800
stay...

18
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:48,000
ay is at the end!

19
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:50,440
Now it's your turn!

20
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:51,840
Here's the word...

21
00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:55,100
ai or ay?

22
00:00:56,440 --> 00:00:59,560
It's ai — because it's in the middle!

23
00:01:00,520 --> 00:01:04,980
Remember: ai in the middle, ay at the end.

24
00:01:05,740 --> 00:01:06,540
Easy, right?

25
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:12,620
Get the English Learning app — where kids learn English the fun way!
